   "summary": "The Food and Drug Administration (FDA, Agency, or we) is issuing a direct final rule that substitutes references to \"animal\" tests or studies with \"nonclinical\" tests or studies, adds a definition of the terms \"nonclinical test\" and \"nonclinical study,\" and makes other comparable or conforming amendments in certain safety and reporting sections of its regulations. The direct final rule also substitutes \"nonclinical\" for \"preclinical\" and \"in vitro\" for consistency in terminology. The Agency is issuing these amendments directly as a final rule because we believe they are noncontroversial changes in terminology that are not expected to affect industry practice and FDA anticipates no…",
